course: dictionary
lesson: 15339
title: Softhearted and hard-hearted
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A softhearted person is kind and gentle. They feel sorry when others are sad or in trouble, and they want to help. «Mia gave her lunch to the new girl, who had forgotten hers.» Mia is softhearted.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Feeling sorry, giving and helping all point to kindness. Test your meaning in the sentence: "Mia is kind and gentle" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Sometimes softhearted has a warning. «The softhearted guard let the stranger in, and the stranger stole the jewels.» Here the guard was so kind that he was easy to persuade. The opposite is hard-hearted, which means cold and not moved by other people's pain.
fact: Softhearted means kind, gentle and easily feels sorry for others.
fact: «Softhearted» can also mean too kind, so that a person is easy to persuade.
fact: The opposite of softhearted is hard-hearted, which means cold and unfeeling.
fact: Softhearted is an adjective, so it describes a person: softhearted, more softhearted, most softhearted.
fact: A softhearted person cares about others, while a hard-hearted person does not seem to care.
exercise: «Mia gave her lunch to the new girl, who had forgotten hers.» What does softhearted suggest about Mia? | Very tall | *Kind and ready to help | Angry and rude | Always late
exercise: «The softhearted old lady forgave the boy who broke her window.» What does softhearted mean here? | Hungry for cake | Strict and angry | Fast at running | *Kind and quick to forgive
exercise: Which word is the opposite of softhearted? | Sleepy | Kind | *Hard-hearted | Gentle
test: Ravi's dad is softhearted. Which action shows this best? | He sells his car | He never notices anyone in trouble | He shouts at stray dogs | *He takes in a lost kitten and feeds it
test: «The softhearted guard let the stranger in, and the stranger stole the jewels.» Why was the guard tricked? | He was asleep all day | *He was too kind and easy to persuade | He was too tall to see the stranger | He was hard-hearted and cruel
exam: Which sentence uses softhearted correctly? | Softhearted the bus ran very quickly. | *The softhearted nurse sat with the crying child. | The softhearted rock is very heavy and grey. | She softhearted the window with a red pen.
